= Pride of the Pitts - Tank Fitters

The FOTF HQ is part fortress, part museum.  They have aquaculture artifacts dating back as far as 18th century Earth.  This building was one of the last bastions of the stakeholder's revolt and hatred of the Megacorps is the saltwater in their veins.  The feeling is mutual but everyone needs to eat so even the Big 3 will hire the Tank Fitters when they have no other choice.


- @mutual_aid
- @public_aid
- @sector_integration
- @gotv

@mutual_aid
title: The Order's tool cribs
subtitle: Gear pooling and reciprocal lending among the tank crews
choose-if: worker_actions_remaining > 0 or month_actions_remaining > 0
unavailable-subtitle: [! if worker_actions_remaining > 0: No worker actions left ?][! if month_actions_remaining > 0: No generic actions left ?]No organizing actions left this month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spendWorkerActionWithFallback();
Q.bumpBlockProsperity('Pitts', 'first', 0.05);
if (typeof Q.syncProsperityDisplays === 'function') { Q.syncProsperityDisplays() }
!}

A fitter's kit is half their livelihood and the other half is knowing who owes you a favor.  The communal cribs stretch both: borrow the rig you can't afford, bank the goodwill for the month the pumps fail on your watch instead of someone else's.

@public_aid
title: Open the workshop doors
subtitle: Help the district, depends on the Order's prosperity
choose-if: worker_actions_remaining > 0 or month_actions_remaining > 0
unavailable-subtitle: [! if worker_actions_remaining > 0: No worker actions left ?][! if month_actions_remaining > 0: No generic actions left ?]No organizing actions left this month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spendWorkerActionWithFallback();
// Requires: Q.prosperity_first > average district prosperity
Q.bumpBlockProsperity('Pitts', 'first', 0.03);
Q.bumpBlockProsperity('Pitts', 'drone', 0.02);
if (typeof Q.syncProsperityDisplays === 'function') { Q.syncProsperityDisplays() }
!}

The Order is doing better than most in the Pitts and it shows.  Non-members get their torn net-seams welded and their dead pumps rebuilt at cost, and nobody asks too many questions about where the spare parts came from.

